# deployed-contracts/ (the per-network launch ledgers scripts/launch.js
# writes to) and deployments/ (the per-network platform-contract addresses
# scripts/deploy.js writes to) are deliberately NOT ignored here — they're
# the record of what's actually been deployed/launched on each network,
# which is the point of keeping them. If you'd rather one not live in git
# (e.g. once it's large, or once a real database has replaced it), add it
# to this file yourself.
